# Never commit `.codegen`

- Do not `git add`, commit, or push `.codegen/` (the local `zero-codegen` tool and merged config).
- `.codegen/` is listed in `.gitignore`. Do not force-add it (`-f`) or remove that ignore rule.
- If codegen files appear in `git status`, unstage them. Copy the tool from the scaffold locally when needed; do not vendor it on GitHub.
